# API base URL (Vite: import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL)
#
# Leave unset for:
#   - Local dev: app uses same-origin paths (/api, /trainer, /runs, …); Vite proxies to the backend.
#   - Production: frontend and API served behind one origin (e.g. nginx routes /api to the API).
#
# Set when the SPA and API are on different origins, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
#
# No trailing slash. Do not commit secrets.

# --- Contact / Founders (optional) ---
#
# VITE_FOUNDER_EMAIL — Your public inbox (shown in mailto links; not a secret).
#   1. Create a file named `.env` in this project root (same folder as package.json).
#   2. Add one line, with your real address, for example:
#        VITE_FOUNDER_EMAIL=alex@yourdomain.com
#   3. Restart `npm run dev` so Vite picks it up.
#   Used by: Founders “Reach out”, and the Contact form when Web3Forms isn’t configured.
#
# VITE_FOUNDER_EMAIL=you@example.com

# VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY — Optional. Get a free key at https://web3forms.com — sends the Contact form to your
# email without opening the user’s mail app. If unset, Contact uses mailto + VITE_FOUNDER_EMAIL instead.
# VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
